/-!
# The C.5.13 dual offender conclusions on both source levels

The canonical auxiliary quotient carries the full original dual offender
bounds. Restricting to the literal moved module I=[V₁,L] preserves the
quadratic action and its rank budget. In the natural branch this gives the
printed dual quadratic-ratio bound; in the A₅ branch the even diagonal
actor gives the same q≤2 conclusion. The odd pair transpositions are kept
outside K₁* as required by the source. The same L-image acts faithfully
on I and its dual, without removing the possible central layer of I.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith C.5.13, printed pp.162–163.
-/
